{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse","id":1534482,"title":"Fake werewolf curse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-20T00:59:42-07:00","id":1534482,"title":"Fake werewolf curse","content":"Im wondering what spheres would you needd to curse a human with a fake traditional werewolf curse:<br /> - you turn every full moon - time 4<br /> - you turn into a werewolf hybrid - life3 /life 5 (depends on if we count transforming into a mostly humanoid big monster a complex transformation or not)<br /> - frenzy on transformation - mind 2<br /> - constant regeneration - life 3??<br /> - cursed bite - ???<br /> <br /> Any ideas or corrections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-20-2024, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T13:41:36-07:00","id":1534606,"title":"","content":"Cursed BIte: I would say Prime 5 + the whole <b>Fake werewolf curse</b><br /> <br /> The idea would be to transform the human into a Living Talisman that can create fake werewolves. The action to activate the Talisman it's &quot;on bite&quot;. You would need at least Life 4* to pass the curse this way<br /> <br /> The bitten werewolves are going to be unable to create new werewolves, unless the Living Talisman it's enchanted so it can create other Living Talismans, which I think it's a bit outside the rules (mostly because a single Arete roll it's never going to net you enough successes to cast such a rote - can Talismans &quot;ritual cast&quot;?, I'm not too sure). At the very least it would have to include the power to consume and store Quintessence to actually cast the &quot;complete&quot; curse, but Prime 5 can do that too.<br /> <br /> *Life 3 body argumentation works on self, with 4 you can cause others to grow claws and fangs. 5 if you want to emphasise the &quot;big monster&quot; part, I'm not 100% sure, but I think 4 doesn't allow to change size and shape radically (so Life 4 would look like old movies werewolves, more than Garou)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T23:01:33-07:00","id":1534621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534606#post1534606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Life 3 body argumentation works on self, with 4 you can cause others to grow claws and fangs. 5 if you want to emphasise the &quot;big monster&quot; part, I'm not 100% sure, but I think 4 doesn't allow to change size and shape radically (so Life 4 would look like old movies werewolves, more than Garou)</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt extra mass just prime 2 added? Its mentioned somewhere in the book with the claws example. You create mass from quintesence ans so can be bigger transforming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T07:11:29-07:00","id":1534631,"title":"","content":"The distinction with radical changes has less to do with mass and more to do with form. The line is blurry, but the examples usually don't count size changes as radical transformations. Presumably a big enough size change would count, but whether quadrupling the weight counts is a decision for the table.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't need Prime 2 to add mass because Mage isn't trying to preserve conservation of mass and energy. That's why mages can enhance or suppress fires with just Forces, and grow wings with just Life. Those spells take patterns that already exist and altering them. Prime 2 is involved when mages create new patterns that don't already exist. It is drawing in quintessence to weave that new pattern.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, if we did decide to conserve mass and energy, Prime 2 would need to be added to <i>a lot</i> of spells that don't currently use it and that's a lot of unnecessary bookkeeping.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T07:21:38-07:00","id":1534632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534631#post1534631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distinction with radical changes has less to do with mass and more to do with form. The line is blurry, but the examples usually don't count size changes as radical transformations. Presumably a big enough size change would count, but whether quadrupling the weight counts is a decision for the table.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't need Prime 2 to add mass because Mage isn't trying to preserve conservation of mass and energy. That's why mages can enhance or suppress fires with just Forces, and grow wings with just Life. Those spells take patterns that already exist and altering them. Prime 2 is involved when mages create new patterns that don't already exist. It is drawing in quintessence to weave that new pattern.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, if we did decide to conserve mass and energy, Prime 2 would need to be added to <i>a lot</i> of spells that don't currently use it and that's a lot of unnecessary bookkeeping.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I must say i dont really get it<br /> Changing into an ant or a tiger is not a radical change and going crinos is? How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-24-2024, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T08:39:15-07:00","id":1534646,"title":"","content":"No, changing into an ant or tiger is definitely a radical change. Species changes are specifically the domain of full Transformation, which is Life 5 to change others. Changing into a werewolf is harder to determine.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, most of the changes into Crinos fall under Alteration. Claws, fur, fangs, even size. Changing a 90lb contortionist into a 450lb professional wrestler isn't out of the question (though different gaming tables may decide differently). Theoretically all of this can be done to others at Life 4.<br /> <br /> For my part, though, I would still go with Life 5, both because of the degree of change and because with Life 5 you can include impossible biology like firebreathing or transformation. That is, with Life 4/Time 4/Other you could inflict an alteration curse that turns on at the full moon. With Life 5/Time 4/Other you could permanently make someone a creature that transforms under the full moon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T10:03:05-07:00","id":1534651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534646#post1534646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, changing into an ant or tiger is definitely a radical change. Species changes are specifically the domain of full Transformation, which is Life 5 to change others. Changing into a werewolf is harder to determine.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, most of the changes into Crinos fall under Alteration. Claws, fur, fangs, even size. Changing a 90lb contortionist into a 450lb professional wrestler isn't out of the question (though different gaming tables may decide differently). Theoretically all of this can be done to others at Life 4.<br /> <br /> For my part, though, I would still go with Life 5, both because of the degree of change and because with Life 5 you can include impossible biology like firebreathing or transformation. That is, with Life 4/Time 4/Other you could inflict an alteration curse that turns on at the full moon. With Life 5/Time 4/Other you could permanently make someone a creature that transforms under the full moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a rote in 2ed that says changing yourself into a tiger is life 4.<br /> <br /> As for Life 5 i never get the &quot;change into anything&quot;. You can do that with 4 + other spheres. Want fire breath? get some forces and life 4. Not really a fan of the you must have a higher sphere to do something to others<br /> <br /> Im starting to think life needs a rework. Something like:<br /> 1. Detect life, scan lifeforms<br /> 2. Modify flesh, cure illness<br /> 3. Modify bones, heal, rise physical attributes, harm life<br /> 4. Modify nerves and hormones<br /> 5. Ressurection, spark of life (as in creating life and with other spheres making other patterns alive), turning of power limiters<br /> <br /> So in this case you want to change your appearence, gain fur? Life 2. Want different bonestructure like claws or turn your hands into wings? Life 3. Want extra limbs or more complicated transformations? life 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T13:17:39-07:00","id":1534660,"title":"","content":"Changing yourself into a tiger is Life 4 in M20 as well. Changing someone else is Life 5, which may not be the most graceful way of balancing the sphere, but I think the point is less that doing things to others should be harder and more that doing things to yourself should be easier. All of the pattern spheres are clunky, though.<br /> <br /> The distinction I was making earlier, though, is that Life 5 allows permanent changes and I've been interpreting that to mean changes that last beyond the end of the spell as opposed to expire when the spell expires. <br /> <br /> I think if I were going to rework Life I would rework all the Pattern Spheres to work in similar ways. I'm hesitant to base too much around what is being changed, and I'd really only look at simple vs complex rather than bone vs nerve or liquid vs solid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T16:04:29-07:00","id":1534664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534660#post1534660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing yourself into a tiger is Life 4 in M20 as well. Changing someone else is Life 5, which may not be the most graceful way of balancing the sphere, but I think the point is less that doing things to others should be harder and more that doing things to yourself should be easier. All of the pattern spheres are clunky, though.<br /> <br /> The distinction I was making earlier, though, is that Life 5 allows permanent changes and I've been interpreting that to mean changes that last beyond the end of the spell as opposed to expire when the spell expires.<br /> <br /> I think if I were going to rework Life I would rework all the Pattern Spheres to work in similar ways. I'm hesitant to base too much around what is being changed, and I'd really only look at simple vs complex rather than bone vs nerve or liquid vs solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need only double successes (forged by dragon fire) or 6 successes (m20) depending on the rule to make magic permament if i remember the rules right. Sphere lvl does not matter.<br /> The thing with complex vs simple is not well defined. If anything i would say flesh is simpler than bone and bone simpler than nerves.<br /> If doing things to yourself is easyer it should be reflected in successes needed not sphere level. Sphere level is Complexity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-24-2024, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T19:41:13-07:00","id":1534673,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s indefinite duration. The transformation still lasts until the spell ends, the spell just never ends. I\u2019ve been interpreting that permanency line in Life 5 as meaning the spell is instant and the change permanent.<br /> <br /> The other two interpretations are that Life spells can\u2019t be indefinite/permanent until Life 5 or Life 5 has an undefined capacity to be permanent outside the normal rules. Neither of those make much sense.<br /> <br /> I agree with both your other complaints. Success level would be a better way to handle self vs other and complexity is not well defined. The divide largely seems to be one of cold blooded vs warm blooded or vertebrate vs invertebrate but it varies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T20:40:43-07:00","id":1534674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534651#post1534651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a rote in 2ed that says changing yourself into a tiger is life 4.<br /> <br /> As for Life 5 i never get the &quot;change into anything&quot;. You can do that with 4 + other spheres. Want fire breath? get some forces and life 4. Not really a fan of the you must have a higher sphere to do something to others<br /> <br /> Im starting to think life needs a rework. Something like:<br /> 1. Detect life, scan lifeforms<br /> 2. Modify flesh, cure illness<br /> 3. Modify bones, heal, rise physical attributes, harm life<br /> 4. Modify nerves and hormones<br /> 5. Ressurection, spark of life (as in creating life and with other spheres making other patterns alive), turning of power limiters<br /> <br /> So in this case you want to change your appearence, gain fur? Life 2. Want different bonestructure like claws or turn your hands into wings? Life 3. Want extra limbs or more complicated transformations? life 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm right up there with you. I too am not a fan of &quot;do it to others&quot; requirements of an extra Sphere level. &quot;Do it to others&quot; is already embraced in the table of successes needed, as you need ZERO additional successes to target yourself, but 1 extra success for any other target. Not to mention that there are plenty Spheres that have no such arbitrary requirements. Do you want to get a &quot;lucky shot&quot; using Entropy 2? Fine, that's zero extra successes to target yourself, or 1 additional success per extra target other than yourself; you don't need Entropy 3 to give good or bad luck to others.<br /> <br /> The only Sphere upon which I fully agree that there should be a difference in levels to target self and others is Mind, because we can actually change our own minds merely with our thoughts directly, without even using Magic. So, it does makes sense that I can make myself smarter using just Mind 1 or create a mental shield with just Mind 1 - because I'm actually in direct control of my own mind! However, in order to do the same with others, you have to sort of &quot;mind rape&quot; them (and that would be the term, even if what your doing is for their own good, you still have to get inside their minds and twist it for your purposes). So, requiring as much as Mind 4 (which is what allows you to really &quot;mess up&quot; - or &quot;reeducate&quot; - somebody else's mind) makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> Even for Life thou, I cannot just simply wish a disease away or instantly heal wounds with happy thoughts. Much less can I jump from a roof with a strong conviction that I can turn into a bird, no matter how much I identify as a bird and deny reality. Our own body is &quot;external&quot; to our &quot;personal being&quot;, which is our mind. Everything we are is inside our mind, our body is just the &quot;hardware&quot; that contains it, and much like a computer can't just simply decide to upgrade his transistors, neither can we consciously desire our body to change. Therefore, it doesn't make any sense for it to be one level easier to target, when it is already easier to target yourself in a required successes base.<br /> <br /> As for rewriting Life, yes, I'm fully in favor. Not just of that, but one of the other problems I have with Life is that you can't really create NEW LIFE. I mean sure, you can create weird stuff on you sanctum lab, but those are pretty much unique monstrosities.<br /> <br /> For all of the talk about &quot;genetics&quot; for the Techie boys, their version of &quot;genetics&quot; seem to be pretty dumb, since our proud boys in black coats are unable to create newly genetically modified species.<br /> <br /> Life's fatal flaw is: your creations cannot procreate.<br /> <br /> That's what I have always think that was missing for Life 5. I believe that Life 5 should allow your lab pets to pass on their &quot;genes&quot; (or &quot;pleura&quot; or whatever mystical-babble equivalent).<br /> <br /> Yes I know, dread all the &quot;Ubermensch&quot; super boys in black, genetically modified to become the &quot;Homo superior&quot; new species but hey, that just makes it even better...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T20:54:29-07:00","id":1534676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534660#post1534660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The distinction I was making earlier, though, is that Life 5 allows permanent changes and I've been interpreting that to mean changes that last beyond the end of the spell as opposed to expire when the spell expires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem thou, there are already rules about how to make effects become permanent. It's in the very same table that I'm ALWAYS pointing towards to talk about most of the silliness of the writing of the Spheres. It's the table about reach, duration and successes required.<br /> <br /> In that table, you need at least 2x more successes to make a change permanent. Could be more (ST fiat).<br /> <br /> Point is, you shouldn't have to need a Sphere at lvl 5 just for that. You certainly don't (necessarily) need Prime 5 to turn something into a permanent talisman, forever rewriting that pattern entirely. What's more, with Entropy 4 you CAN (with enough successes) permanently &quot;bless&quot; or &quot;curse&quot; a person even if said person is still in the womb.<br /> <br /> So again, that's just another arbitrary and rather nonsensical limitation from the part of the writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T23:46:40-07:00","id":1534682,"title":"","content":"Can you point to the table?<br /> <br /> The gene thing is interesting. Not really too useful in game terms but interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534673#post1534673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s indefinite duration. The transformation still lasts until the spell ends, the spell just never ends. I\u2019ve been interpreting that permanency line in Life 5 as meaning the spell is instant and the change permanent.<br /> <br /> The other two interpretations are that Life spells can\u2019t be indefinite/permanent until Life 5 or Life 5 has an undefined capacity to be permanent outside the normal rules. Neither of those make much sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont really see the difference between indefinite and permament. Mage tries to lump many wierd things in 4 and 5 when the writers did not have a good idea what to put in. I also personally have trouble with adding the shapeshift aspect in 5 but limiting permamency for this sphere alone seems redundant. The genes thing seems like a better idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T07:22:38-07:00","id":1534689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534676#post1534676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the problem thou, there are already rules about how to make effects become permanent. It's in the very same table that I'm ALWAYS pointing towards to talk about most of the silliness of the writing of the Spheres. It's the table about reach, duration and successes required.<br /> <br /> In that table, you need at least 2x more successes to make a change permanent. Could be more (ST fiat).<br /> <br /> Point is, you shouldn't have to need a Sphere at lvl 5 just for that. You certainly don't (necessarily) need Prime 5 to turn something into a permanent talisman, forever rewriting that pattern entirely. What's more, with Entropy 4 you CAN (with enough successes) permanently &quot;bless&quot; or &quot;curse&quot; a person even if said person is still in the womb.<br /> <br /> So again, that's just another arbitrary and rather nonsensical limitation from the part of the writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a given value of permanent, yes. What the chart doesn't make clear is if permanent means the spell is permanent but the effect ends if the spell is dispelled or if the effect is permanent even after the spell ends. Nor, for that matter, does the Life 5 writeup make it clear if it is referring to the permanency in the charts or something else. As I said, there are other ways of interpreting Life 5, they just make less sense to me. <br /> <br /> Of course, the reference to permanency in Life 5 may be yet another remnant of a previous draft that slipped through editing. There's a lot of that in M20 and even more in HDYDT.<br /> <br /> In most games I don't think the distinction between permanent spells and permanent effects will come into play so I don't know how important it is. That said, let me give an edge case. <br /> <br /> Doctor &quot;I Just Get These Headaches&quot; (henceforth referred to as Dr Head) decides to make a bunch of these werewolf approximations. The first (subject A) he generates in a lab from nothing. It's a pure creation spell. The next two he makes from helpful &quot;volunteers&quot; he &quot;volunteered&quot; into the back of his white van. For subject B, Dr Head only rolls enough successes for a six month duration. For subject C, he gets enough successes for the spell to be permanent.<br /> <br /> Subject B is clearly under the effects of a spell. When the spell runs out, his werewolf affliction ends and he goes back to being a normal person. If the spell is dispelled early, he goes back to being a normal person early. Subject A, though, is probably not under the effect of a spell. He just exists now and is not subject to being dispelled. At least we generally don't think of created people being subject to that. I think a few of the Technocracy books have mages that were initially created in a lab before they awakened, and they probably weren't intended to be one successful unweaving away from death.<br /> <br /> Subject C, though, is tricky. On the one hand his condition should be permanent like subject A. On the other hand he was created like subject B, which means the spell should function like that of subject B, just with a permanent duration. Not only that, but if he is like B, there should be a way Dr Head could make him like A instead. If it isn't rolling enough successes, what is it? If it is rolling enough successes, what is the threshold for permanent effect vs unending spell?<br /> <br /> Is this an important question? I have no idea. Will it arise at some gaming tables? Definitely.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T11:28:14-07:00","id":1534853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534689#post1534689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a given value of permanent, yes. What the chart doesn't make clear is if permanent means the spell is permanent but the effect ends if the spell is dispelled or if the effect is permanent even after the spell ends. Nor, for that matter, does the Life 5 writeup make it clear if it is referring to the permanency in the charts or something else. As I said, there are other ways of interpreting Life 5, they just make less sense to me.<br /> <br /> Of course, the reference to permanency in Life 5 may be yet another remnant of a previous draft that slipped through editing. There's a lot of that in M20 and even more in HDYDT.<br /> <br /> In most games I don't think the distinction between permanent spells and permanent effects will come into play so I don't know how important it is. That said, let me give an edge case.<br /> <br /> Doctor &quot;I Just Get These Headaches&quot; (henceforth referred to as Dr Head) decides to make a bunch of these werewolf approximations. The first (subject A) he generates in a lab from nothing. It's a pure creation spell. The next two he makes from helpful &quot;volunteers&quot; he &quot;volunteered&quot; into the back of his white van. For subject B, Dr Head only rolls enough successes for a six month duration. For subject C, he gets enough successes for the spell to be permanent.<br /> <br /> Subject B is clearly under the effects of a spell. When the spell runs out, his werewolf affliction ends and he goes back to being a normal person. If the spell is dispelled early, he goes back to being a normal person early. Subject A, though, is probably not under the effect of a spell. He just exists now and is not subject to being dispelled. At least we generally don't think of created people being subject to that. I think a few of the Technocracy books have mages that were initially created in a lab before they awakened, and they probably weren't intended to be one successful unweaving away from death.<br /> <br /> Subject C, though, is tricky. On the one hand his condition should be permanent like subject A. On the other hand he was created like subject B, which means the spell should function like that of subject B, just with a permanent duration. Not only that, but if he is like B, there should be a way Dr Head could make him like A instead. If it isn't rolling enough successes, what is it? If it is rolling enough successes, what is the threshold for permanent effect vs unending spell?<br /> <br /> Is this an important question? I have no idea. Will it arise at some gaming tables? Definitely.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. In my opinion, this &quot;permanent duration&quot; should mean &quot;the Pattern of the target is permanently changed&quot;. When you create a Talisman, you've permanently changed the Pattern of the object. &quot;Permanent spells&quot; should be like amputating an army; you permanently changed the Pattern of the subject. Therefore, if you add enough successes to make a &quot;permanent&quot; change into a spider to turn it into an ant with Life 2, that ant is no longer a spider anymore, its Pattern has been irrevocably changed into that of an ant. If you take an ordinary knife and turns it into a &quot;healing dagger&quot; Talisman, its etherial Pattern is irrevocably changed, the dagger's capabilities of healing are now part of what that dagger is, much like my lungs and liver are irrevocable parts of my current alive Pattern (and ripping them off of me would change my Pattern to &quot;deceased&quot;).<br /> <br /> That's hinted throughout the entire texts of the books from at least the 2nd edition and forward, there are several entries with &quot;unless you permanently change the Pattern of the target&quot; and similar.<br /> <br /> But... I may be wrong, maybe that's not what the writers originally meant. Imho however, that's the interpretation that I find to make most sense, but I did understand what you meant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T07:31:45-07:00","id":1534894,"title":"","content":"That's the way I did and sometimes still do look at it. I don't think I ever recognized the difference until awakening came out and the arguments over whether it was reasonable that true permanency should cost a WP dot (back before it was clear replacing a spent WP dot cost a single XP). The text of Life 5 recently had me revisiting the issue.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it doesn't make too much of a difference in Ascension, especially if we don't use the optional unweaving rules. Narratively, though, there are lots of stories where a spell causes a permanent change (Roald Dahl's The Witches, The Emperor's New Groove, etc) but lots of others where the spell is clearly ongoing because there are ways of breaking the curse (Beauty and the Beast, Lord of the Rings, Shrek). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T09:24:12-07:00","id":1534904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1534894#post1534894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the way I did and sometimes still do look at it. I don't think I ever recognized the difference until awakening came out and the arguments over whether it was reasonable that true permanency should cost a WP dot (back before it was clear replacing a spent WP dot cost a single XP). The text of Life 5 recently had me revisiting the issue.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it doesn't make too much of a difference in Ascension, especially if we don't use the optional unweaving rules. Narratively, though, there are lots of stories where a spell causes a permanent change (Roald Dahl's The Witches, The Emperor's New Groove, etc) but lots of others where the spell is clearly ongoing because there are ways of breaking the curse (Beauty and the Beast, Lord of the Rings, Shrek).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the case of poorly written and vague game mechanics. I have no doubt that the writers wanted to include the possibility of &quot;permanent permanent&quot; changes, like I said, by the means of the multiple entries about &quot;unless you permanently change the target's Pattern&quot;, but I don't think this comes with the exclusion of &quot;dispelled permanent&quot;, or in a better way to say it, a spell that is held on the target by an endless amount of time without actually permanently changing the target's Pattern.<br /> <br /> And now that I'm thinking about it, I believe this is actually what the writers initially intended... And to show that, we do my favorite game of all times, which is to always go back to the tables for Duration, Damage, Required Successes and Correspondence Reach.<br /> <br /> As it stands, if memory serves, in the 2ed, this table showed that, for 6+ extra successes thrown into extending the duration of a spell, there's no &quot;clear limit&quot;. The text also says something like, and I'm paraphrasing, &quot;at the ST's discretion, double the amount of successes for the effect could make it permanent&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, if memory serves, this was also present on the Rev (3ed) table too.<br /> <br /> I think that this text was a bit vague - heck, in fact I always thought so about those rules contained in the tables, that it was too vague - but what this seems to imply is that, a spell can be turned &quot;permanent&quot; by adding 6+ successes to an effect, but that a PATTERN CHANGE (&quot;permanent permanent) can be achieved if you add 2x the amount of successes required for creating the effect in the first place.<br /> <br /> The text is somewhat vague, and this was thrown in as just a small note bellow the tables, instead of being in the larger body of text in the rules section, so that's why I believe it got a bit confusing and most of the time overlooked, but now that I'm thinking about it, I believe that the original intent of the writers was to have this exact interpretation, 6+ successes for permanently holding a spell on a target (therefore being prone to being dispelled or nullified) and 2x successes for a permanent change of the Pattern of a target (therefore, NOT dispellable, since the alteration is truly permanent at a fundamental level).<br /> <br /> Too bad those rules weren't explicitly stated, and even worse, were claimed to be &quot;at the discretion of the ST&quot;, which apparently had the effect of making the entire player community to consider them as optional rules at best and almost &quot;gold rule&quot; non canon house rules at worst. When I personally believe that what was meant was &quot;those tables are general guidelines that could be adjusted by ST fiat. Herculean effects may require more successes; making an island float MIGHT require more than just 6 extra successes to make it permanent, however as a general rule for &quot;regular normal&quot; spells, apply the basic rule of 6 extra successes to make a spell permanent&quot;. My understanding is that this miscommunication has been occuring exactly because the text isn't clear enough about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T19:56:08-07:00","id":1535478,"title":"","content":"Meh, if you're going to use WW in M:tA, I'd always make them out to M:tA rules. No gifts, only Spheres etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T23:44:47-07:00","id":1535483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1535478#post1535478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, if you're going to use WW in M:tA, I'd always make them out to M:tA rules. No gifts, only Spheres etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nobody said otherwise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T23:22:07-07:00","id":1535502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1535478#post1535478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, if you're going to use WW in M:tA, I'd always make them out to M:tA rules. No gifts, only Spheres etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is talking here about any gifts.<br /> <br /> But i still would dissagree. I prefer to use my mix of other splat systems for nonmage creatures. Not everything has to be the same power system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T17:14:09-07:00","id":1535877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534482-fake-werewolf-curse?p=1535502#post1535502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one is talking here about any gifts.<br /> <br /> But i still would dissagree. I prefer to use my mix of other splat systems for nonmage creatures. Not everything has to be the same power system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we've done that a lot. Mixing splats other players don't know about, like KotE, in their system, can add some mystery to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}